\f0\b\fs22 \cf2 Specification Interview \'97 Round 1: Core Vision\

\f1\b0 I'll ask questions in focused rounds. Answer what you can, say "not sure" where you haven't decided \'97 that's fine, I'll offer options.\
1. Product type and delivery format:\uc0\u8232 What is the end product? Specifically:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}A\'a0VST3/AU plugin\'a0that runs inside a DAW (Logic, Ableton, Reaper, etc.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2. Platform targets:\uc0\u8232 Which operating systems and architectures must the final product support?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}macOS (Apple Silicon)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Windows (x64)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 3. The one-sentence pitch:\uc0\u8232 In plain language, what does this software\'a0do\'a0for the user?\
I would like to create a series of spatial audio VST plugins which utilize the same core spatial audio processing algorithm(s) and output to several standard speaker layouts, starting with a delay plugin where each repeat occurs at a different, definable position. A great example to look at is Sound Particles\'92 inDelay VST. \
4. Who is the user?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}All of the listed users except the \'93consumer/listener.\'94 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 5. Channel architecture:\uc0\u8232 Your existing code is set up for 64 discrete channels. Is that the actual target, or was 64 just a stress test? What spatial format are you targeting?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}64 channels was a stress test, but is the maximum number of audio channels. Ideally the number of channels should be defined the track which the plugin is placed on, with a maximum of 64. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\
\

\f0\b Round 2: Spatial Engine & The Delay Plugin\

\f1\b0 \
6. Spatialization method \'97 this is the most important architectural decision:\uc0\u8232 There are several ways to position a sound in a speaker array. Each has trade-offs:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}The hybrid model is the most ideal solution here, but I would love for the user to have the option of which algorithm to use, not just Ambisonics. Meaning, the user could select VBAP, VBIP, Ambisonics (HOA), KNN, or others (see the Spat library from Ircam for other common algorithms) and then it will decode to standard speaker formats. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Do you have a preference, or would you like my recommendation?\
7. Target output layouts \'97 you mentioned "several standard speaker layouts":\uc0\u8232 Which of these do you consider must-haves for v1?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Let\'92s start with a binaural output for v0.1, once proven we will then move onto surround configurations\'97quadrophonic, 5.1, 7.1, and 9.1. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 8. The spatial delay specifically \'97 let me confirm the creative behavior:\uc0\u8232 In a plugin like inDelay, each delay repeat has a\'a0position\'a0in 3D space. A few sub-questions:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}There should certainly be a visual map, but I think most users would rather use presets, such as specific types of trajectories you mentioned. This then implies that there must be a preset loading and saving system, which ultimately means that a user can manually place the position of each repeat for the purpose of saving a preset. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 9. The plugin suite roadmap:\uc0\u8232 You said this is the first plugin in a series. What other effect types are you envisioning? For example:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Spatial reverb? - yes\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Spatial granular / particle effects? - yes\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Spatial panner / object placer? - yes, but something more like Sound Particles\'92 Energy Panner\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Spatial chorus/flanger? - yes\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 10. UI expectations:\
Do you have a visual style in mind (dark/minimal, skeuomorphic, futuristic)?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}a 2D top-down/front-view is likely sufficient for all iterations, again like the Sound Particles\'92 inDelay plugin.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Any reference UIs you like the look of (from any plugin, not just spatial)? SnappySnap by Electric Smudge has a great UI as well. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\

\f0\b Round 3: Implementation Details & Remaining Gaps\

\f1\b0 \
11. Per-tap delay controls:\uc0\u8232 Beyond spatial position, what parameters should each individual delay tap have?\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Delay time (absolute ms or tempo-synced note value)? Yes, both.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Feedback amount per tap, or one global feedback that feeds back into the spatial trajectory? Let\'92s start with one global feedback knob.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Filter (high-cut / low-cut per tap to simulate distance attenuation)? Yes, but we\'92ll start with one global filter, and in v2 we\'92ll add some filtering controls like on Eventide\'92s Blackhole Immersive.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Level per tap? No, just a global Dry/Wet knob and global Input and Output volume knobs. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Pitch shift per tap? This is an interesting concept. For v1 let\'92s start with a global pitch control, so that each delay is increased or decreased by the set semitone amount.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Any other per-tap effects? Global modulation effects, such as pitch modulation with an LFO, or global chorus effects. Neither of these are needed for v1 and could be added later. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 12. Tempo sync:\uc0\u8232 Should delay times be lockable to the host DAW's tempo? (e.g., quarter note, dotted eighth, triplet, etc.) This is standard for delay plugins \'97 just confirming it's expected. - Yes absolutely. There should be the ability to lock it to the DAW tempo or set the time via milliseconds. \
13. Maximum tap count:\uc0\u8232 How many simultaneous delay taps should the plugin support? Common ranges are 4\'968 for manual placement, or effectively unlimited when driven by feedback. What feels right for this product? I think because most people using this would be on a 7.1.4 Dolby Atmos setup, being able to set 12 manually placed positions would be great so they can, at least, be positioned where each of the speakers is located (of course ignoring the LFE channel, but 12 is a nice even number and allows it to scale for use with Ambisonic domes). \
14. HRTF for binaural \'97 this is a critical technical decision for v0.1:\uc0\u8232 To render spatial positions to headphone output, we need an HRTF (Head-Related Transfer Function) dataset. Options:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Because I do not know very much about this topic in particular, please make a decision, and based on data, research, and user feedback, select 5 total HRTF options from which a user can choose from. In later version we can consider including the ability for users to upload custom HRTFs or even create a separate application which generates them based on data gathered by iPhone scans.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 15. The IRCAM Spat library \'97 use it or reimplement?\uc0\u8232 You referenced IRCAM Spat's algorithms (VBAP, VBIP, KNN, DBAP, etc.). Two paths:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Reimplement the algorithms from published research.\'a0VBAP (Pulkki 1997), DBAP (Lossius 2009), KNN, and Ambisonics encoding are all well-documented in academic literature. Pro: no license fees, full control, optimizable. Con: more development time. Please use this solution as licensing IRCAM\'92s SPAT can be very expensive and we\'92re trying to make a solution which will is inexpensive to purchase for users. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Which direction appeals to you?\
16. Preset system & trajectory engine:\uc0\u8232 You mentioned presets with trajectories (spiral, bounce, etc.). A few specifics:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Should trajectories be\'a0animated in real-time\'a0(taps move during playback) or\'a0static\'a0(positions are fixed once the preset is loaded)? Both options are possible. When movement is applied the Doppler effect could also be applied to the tap positions which move. However, for v1, let\'92s begin with static positions for the taps.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Should trajectory motion be\'a0tempo-synced\'a0to the host BPM? Yes of course. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Do you want a\'a0factory preset library\'a0shipping with the plugin, or is user-created presets sufficient for v0.1? I would like to see only a few basic ones, such as one object where each speaker in a surround deployment is, as a start. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 17. Naming & branding:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Do you have a product name / brand name in mind for the suite? Spatial Media Library\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}What about the delay plugin specifically? OpenSpatialDelay\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}18. Licensing & copy protection:\uc0\u8232 How do you plan to distribute and protect the software? Starting with GitHub, but that is not yet defined. Maybe later it will be sold from a website. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Free / open-source? Open Source to begin with, then maybe a product later. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Commercial with serial number activation? Not yet. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Subscription? Not yet. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}iLok? No.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}No protection (honor system)? For now this is fine. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 19. Build & development environment \'97 moving forward:\uc0\u8232 Your Docker setup proved the toolchain but can't produce macOS/Windows binaries. Going forward:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}macOS builds will need to happen\'a0natively on macOS\'a0(or via CI like GitHub Actions with macOS runners) for AU and code signing.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Windows builds need MSVC or cross-compilation.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Are you comfortable with a\'a0GitHub-based CI/CD pipeline\'a0that builds for both platforms automatically? Yes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 20. Timeline & resourcing:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Do you have a target release date or is this open-ended? Open-ended for now as it is just a hobby project, but I would like to see a usable deliverable before end of March. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Is it just you and me (Claude) building this, or do you have other developers or collaborators? Just you and me for now.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Any budget considerations I should factor into recommendations (e.g., for HRTF datasets, IRCAM licensing, code signing certificates, etc.)? Yes, do everything without incurring additional cost on top of your monthly subscription fee. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\
